{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_e70868b3-2e55-448a-988e-7c94cfeda9c6","role":"user","created":1775342959,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_43d34109f29444b19cbe308e","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"In view of the numerous transfers from the Federal Government to state and local governments and from state governments to local governments, the division of total governmental expenditures among the three governmental levels, after adjustment for these transfers, differs substantially from the division on the basis of expenditures from the various governments' own sources. In 1938, after adjustment for intergovernmental transfers, local expenditures were more than twice as large as state expenditures and exceeded Federal expenditures by approximately $300,000,000. (For the details see Table 3.)\n| Function > Unnamed: 0_level_1 | Expenditures from own sources 1/ > Federal | Expenditures from own sources 1/ > State | Expenditures from own sources 1/ > Local | Expenditures from own sources 1/ > Total | Intergovernmental grants 2/ > Federal to State | Intergovernmental grants 2/ > Federal to Local | Intergovernmental grants 2/ > State to Local | Intergovernmental grants 2/ > Local to State | Expenditures for own functions 3/ > Federal | Expenditures for own functions 3/ > State | Expenditures for own functions 3/ > Local | Expenditures for own functions 3/ > Total |\n3/ Includes expenditures from own sources and from \"Intergovernmental Grants\" received, but excludes grants paid other jurisdictions.","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"In view of the numerous transfers from the Federal Government to state and local governments and from state governments to local governments, the division of total governmental expenditures among the three governmental levels, after adjustment for these transfers, differs substantially from the division on the basis of expenditures from the various governments' own sources. In 1938, after adjustment for intergovernmental transfers, local expenditures were more than twice as large as state expenditures and exceeded Federal expenditures by approximately $300,000,000. (For the details see Table 3.)\n| Function > Unnamed: 0_level_1 | Expenditures from own sources 1/ > Federal | Expenditures from own sources 1/ > State | Expenditures from own sources 1/ > Local | Expenditures from own sources 1/ > Total | Intergovernmental grants 2/ > Federal to State | Intergovernmental grants 2/ > Federal to Local | Intergovernmental grants 2/ > State to Local | Intergovernmental grants 2/ > Local to State | Expenditures for own functions 3/ > Federal | Expenditures for own functions 3/ > State | Expenditures for own functions 3/ > Local | Expenditures for own functions 3/ > Total |\n3/ Includes expenditures from own sources and from \"Intergovernmental Grants\" received, but excludes grants paid other jurisdictions.","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
